{
  "title": "Pipeline step-output reads conflate malformed JSON with missing fields",
  "description": "Steps that read prior step outputs use `.and_then(|v| \
serde_json::from_value(v.clone()).ok())` followed by a None branch whose error \
message claims the field is absent. A malformed-but-present value is \
indistinguishable from a missing one, and the resulting error message lies. \
Examples:\n\
- server/src/scraping/steps.rs:125,293 — `raw_recipe` deserialization failure \
reports \"No raw_recipe in extract output\"\n\
- server/src/scraping/steps.rs:311 — malformed `method_used` silently treated \
as absent, changing version_source\n\
- server/src/scraping/steps.rs:329 — corrupt `photo_ids` silently drops all \
photos from the saved recipe\n\
- server/src/scraping/steps.rs:1015 — corrupt `suggested_tags` silently \
applies no tags\n\
- ramekin-core/src/pipeline/steps/parse_ingredients.rs:59 — same raw_recipe \
pattern\n\
- ramekin-core/src/pipeline/steps/enrich_*.rs — `.unwrap_or(\"\")` on \
title/ingredients/instructions feeds empty strings into AI prompts when \
raw_recipe fields are missing or non-string\n\
\n\
Discovered during the fail-fast audit (p3-fail-fast-audit-swallowed-errors). \
These are lower severity because the step still fails or the enrichment is \
best-effort, but per the fail-fast rule the deserialization error should be \
surfaced distinctly (match on Result and include the serde error in the step \
error) rather than folded into the \"missing\" branch.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 4,
  "type": "task",
  "labels": [
    "server",
    "ramekin-core",
    "error-handling",
  ],
